# Search parameters for the self-driving `auto-optimize` command — tracked
# in git, like run-config.env. Edit, commit, `git pull` on the droplet, then
# `sudo systemctl start eval-auto-optimize` to kick off a fresh search.
#
# This is NOT `enable`d at boot and NOT auto-restarted on failure or
# completion (see eval-auto-optimize.service) — it's a one-off, bounded
# search you trigger by hand, not an always-on service like eval-harness.
#
# Same flags as `python3 scripts/eval_harness.py auto-optimize` — see
# eval/README.md. MUST stay double-quoted — see run-config.env's comment
# for why (this file is bash-`source`d too, not systemd's EnvironmentFile
# format).
#
# --baseline-run must be a run-id that already has completed results (e.g.
# do-batch-2) — auto-optimize learns from that run's actual validator/judge
# failures, it doesn't generate a baseline itself.
AUTO_OPTIMIZE_ARGS="--baseline-run do-batch-2 --rounds 3 --candidates-per-round 6 --concurrency 6 --time-budget-minutes 60"
